@* TextField's Overview, written by hand, after Button's: a sentence and an example per section,
   code alone where a preview would show nothing new (types change the keyboard, not the look).
   Mode support, accessibility and the parameters follow; the API page has the full reference. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A text field is a field for one line of text, such as a name or an email address. It suits short text. It's a native input, so it posts with the form, <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">with JavaScript off</Anchor> too. For several lines, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/text-area">TextArea</Anchor>. For numbers, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/number-field">NumberField</Anchor>. For a password, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/password-field">PasswordField</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and hints</Heading>
<TextBlock>A field's label comes from the model: its <Code>[Display(Name)]</Code>, or the property name in words. <Code>[Required]</Code> adds a required mark. To replace the label, set <Code>Label</Code>; to add help under the field, set <Code>Hint</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-labels" />

<Heading Level="2">Types</Heading>
<TextBlock>A field's type sets the on-screen keyboard, and for email and URL, the browser's check. To make the field an email, phone, URL or search field, set <Code>Type</Code>. The type defaults from <Code>[EmailAddress]</Code>, <Code>[Phone]</Code> and <Code>[Url]</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Types</Code>

<Heading Level="2">Masks</Heading>
<TextBlock>A mask gives the text a fixed form, such as a phone number or a postal code. Set <Code>Mask</Code>. As the user types or pastes, the field drops characters that don't fit and adds the mask's own, such as the brackets and the dash in <Code>(000) 000-0000</Code>. The server does the same when the form posts, so <Code>416.555.0199</Code> posted with JavaScript off binds as <Code>(416) 555-0199</Code>. A value with an empty slot is invalid. Show the format in <Code>Placeholder</Code>, such as <Code>(000) 000-0000</Code>. Screen readers don't hear the mask, and some don't read a placeholder, so when the label doesn't make the format plain, say it in the <Code>Hint</Code> too.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-masks" />
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>In the mask</th><th>Takes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>0</Code>, <Code>9</Code></td><td>A digit; <Code>9</Code> may be left empty</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>L</Code>, <Code>?</Code></td><td>A letter; <Code>?</Code> may be left empty</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>A</Code>, <Code>a</Code></td><td>A letter or digit; <Code>a</Code> may be left empty</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>&amp;</Code>, <Code>C</Code></td><td>Any character but a space; <Code>C</Code> may be left empty</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>&gt;</Code>, <Code>&lt;</Code>, <Code>|</Code></td><td>Letters after it in upper case, in lower case, or as typed</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>\</Code></td><td>Makes the next character part of the text, as <Code>\0</Code></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Anything else</td><td>Itself, added as the user types</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>
<TextBlock>The value binds as shown, <Code>(416) 555-0199</Code>. To bind only the typed characters, <Code>4165550199</Code>, set <Code>RawValue</Code>. To add mask characters of your own, set <Code>MaskRules</Code> to each character and the class it takes, as <Code>new() { ['X'] = "[A-HJ-NP-Z]" }</Code>. A field whose mask has only digits gets the number keyboard on phones.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Icons</Heading>
<TextBlock>A field can show an icon inside it, such as a search icon. Set <Code>StartIcon</Code> or <Code>EndIcon</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-icons" />

<Heading Level="2">A clear button</Heading>
<TextBlock>A clear button empties the field. It shows while the field has a value. Set <Code>Clearable</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-clearable" />
<TextBlock>Every field whose value can be empty has <Code>Clearable</Code>. A <Code>Select</Code> clears back to its <Code>Placeholder</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Add-ons</Heading>
<TextBlock>Add-ons attach text, a <Anchor Href="docs/components/select">Select</Anchor> or a button to the side of the field. Set <Code>StartAddon</Code> or <Code>EndAddon</Code>. A submit button in an add-on posts the form, so a search box works with JavaScript off.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-addons" />

<Heading Level="2">Validation</Heading>
<TextBlock>A field's rules come from the model's attributes. Before the form post, the browser checks required, length, range, email and URL, with your <Code>ErrorMessage</Code>. After it, the server checks every rule and shows its messages under the field.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-validation" />

<Heading Level="2">Sizes, read-only and disabled</Heading>
<TextBlock>To line the field up with buttons and other fields, set <Code>Size</Code>. For a value the user can see but not change, set <Code>ReadOnly</Code>; it still posts. For a value that doesn't post, set <Code>Disabled</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-states" />
<TextBlock>Before trusting a posted value, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#values-a-form-post-can-change">Values a form post can change</Anchor>. Before saving a disabled value from a form post, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#disabled-fields-and-form-posts">Disabled fields and form posts</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>A mask's error comes from the app's text. To set it for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>IzzyText</th><th>Sets</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>MaskIncomplete</Code></td><td>The error for a masked value with an empty slot; <Code>{0}</Code> is the label. <Code>MaskInvalidMessage</Code> sets it for one field</td><td>"The {0} field is incomplete."</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<Heading Level="2">See also</Heading>
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor>: posts on static pages and validates on interactive ones.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/text-area">TextArea</Anchor>: several lines, growing and counting.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/number-field">NumberField</Anchor>: numbers, with stepper buttons.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/password-field">PasswordField</Anchor>: a password, with show and hide and a new one's requirements.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/field-frame">FieldFrame</Anchor>: the same label, hint and errors around a control of your own.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/common/style-props">Style props</Anchor>: <Code>Width</Code>, <Code>Grow</Code> and margins on the whole field.</ListItem>
</List>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @* Label, type and limits from the model's attributes. *@
        <TextField @bind-Value="Model.Email" />

        @* Your own label and a hint. *@
        <TextField @bind-Value="Model.Dept" Label="Department" Hint="On your profile." />

        @* Text attached to the field. *@
        <TextField @bind-Value="Model.Website">
            <StartAddon>https://</StartAddon>
        </TextField>
        """;

    private const string Types = """
        @* [Phone] on the property: type="tel". *@
        <TextField @bind-Value="Model.Phone" />

        <TextField @bind-Value="Model.Query" Type="TextFieldType.Search" />
        """;
}
